  "id": "correlated-samples",
  "term": "correlated samples",
  "definition": "Correlated samples are paired or linked sets of measurements in which the observations are related, such as two measurements taken from the same individuals. In this kind of comparison, analysis focuses on the difference scores between the matched measurements rather than treating the two sets of observations as independent.",
